  "verdict": "NULL: in the shared feature space, no domain combination beats the local model (Protocol A). Cross-domain taste signal, if it exists, must be item-level (entity bridges), not feature-level pooling.",
  "verdict_is_positive": false,
  "zero_shot_verdict": "ZERO-SHOT TRANSFER IS REAL: with NO training data of its own, a target is ranked from other domains alone at a substantial fraction of what a target-only XGB on the same shared features achieves (not the deployed model). Best per target -- tv+game+book->movie rho=+0.496 (74% of a target-only XGB on the same shared features); movie->tv rho=+0.448 (108% of a target-only XGB on the same shared features); movie+book->game rho=+0.553 (138% of a target-only XGB on the same shared features); movie+tv+game->book rho=+0.599 (101% of a target-only XGB on the same shared features). Reported as Spearman rank correlation: the rating distribution is concentrated (62% of films in three adjacent half-star bins), so MAE-based skill barely separates a model from a constant and conflates ordering with calibration."
